ec:\n\n- **`web/src/lib/home.ts`**: added `WATCHER_STOPPED_SENTENCE`, `watcherCallout()` (stopped checked first), and `LiveState` with `liveState()`, which applies down \u2192 stopped \u2192 match \u2192 watching \u2192 idle.\n- **`web/src/shell/LiveStatus.tsx`**: the pill uses `liveState()` and shows \"Watcher stopped\" with a warn dot. The panel shows the stopped sentence in that state. The not-watching paragraph now uses `NOT_WATCHING_SENTENCE`, which has the same wording.\n- **`web/src/views/CurrentMatchView.tsx`**: the no-match branch uses `watcherCallout(live.data)`. The opening-hand, intermission and match branches show the stopped callout first when `watcher_stopped` is set.\n- **`web/src/components/home/FirstRun.tsx`**: `STEPS` is now a function of `live`, and the first step's detail is `watcherCallout(live) ?? NOT_WATCHING_SENTENCE`.\n\nTwo things to know:\n\n- Neither I nor the checks ran the dashboard in a browser, so the visual result of the new callouts is unseen.\n- I did not run the Python suite or the verification commands in `AGENTS.md`, since the spec lists only the web checks and no Python file changed.\n\nI did not commit anything.", "ttft_ms": 1767, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 44101, "uuid": "20baefa8-1062-41d5-b8ce-03fb308610b7", "ttft_stream_ms": 1709, "time_to_request_ms": 379, "first_content_frame_ms": 1709, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
